    "text": "Consider the figure here. A particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;is constrained to move inside a smooth vertical groove of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> and is connected to a light spring of spring constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>&nbsp;in equilibrium. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> is centre of the groove. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math> are horizontal and vertical axes respectively. Different physical parameters are related as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>KR</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>mg</mi></math>. Angular frequency of the oscillations, if the particle is slightly displaced from the shown equilibrium position is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0028_81b274b339fa.jpg\" style=\"width: 230px; height: 419px;\" />"
